# Widget & Component Conventions

## Widget Component Contract

Every widget in `src/components/widgets/` follows this pattern:

- Props: `label`, `value`, `onChange`, optional `tooltip`
- Renders a self-contained field with label + control
- Uses Tailwind classes from the project's `@theme` tokens (surface-*, accent-*)
- No direct model/schema imports — widgets are model-agnostic

## FieldRenderer

`src/components/FieldRenderer.tsx` is the single bridge between schemas and widgets. It:

1. Checks `param.visibility` conditions against current values
2. Switches on `param.widget.type` to pick the right widget component
3. Passes value from `values[param.key]` with fallback to `widget.default`

When adding a new widget type:
1. Add the variant to `FieldWidget` union in `src/types/schema.ts`
2. Create the widget component in `src/components/widgets/`
3. Add one `case` in `FieldRenderer.tsx`

## Styling Rules

- Field containers: `px-4 py-2.5`
- Labels: `text-xs font-medium text-gray-400`
- Inputs: `bg-surface-700 border border-surface-500 text-gray-200 text-xs rounded-md`
- Focus state: `focus:border-accent-green`
- Tooltip indicator: `ⓘ` character with `title` attribute
